# Data conversion between gigabyte and tebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between gigabyte and tebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1GB to 0.0009TiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5GB yields 0.0013TiB; backward, converting 1TiB to 1099.5116GB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5TiB yields 1649.2674GB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1GB
print(forward_whole->to(TiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GB
print(forward_fractional->to(TiB))
backward_whole: int = 1TiB
print(backward_whole->to(GB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TiB
print(backward_fractional->to(GB))

<<< stdout
0.0009TiB
0.0013TiB
1099.5116GB
1649.2674GB

<<< stderr
